    "title": "G.I. car dealership accused of writing bad check to purchase vehicle from another car dealership - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Carol Bryant ,\n6 hours ago GRAND ISLAND – A Grand Island car dealership is accused of writing a bad check for approximately $31,000 to purchase a vehicle from Dick’s Motor Company, 716 W. Fifth St. Grand Island Police Division Chief Dean Elliott said that Dick’s Motor Company had contacted the other car dealership after the check bounced, but payment was not made at that time. That’s when the car dealership reported the incident to police. Read full article\n6",
